      "recap_tekst": "Germany beat Ivory Coast 2-1.\nGoals: Germany — Undav (68, 90+4); Ivory Coast — Kessie (30).\n\nDeniz Undav emerged from the bench to score twice and send Germany through to the FIFA World Cup 2026™ Round of 32.\nEmerse Fae's Côte d'Ivoire were on course to qualify after Franck Kessie's goal on the half hour, but Undav's close-range header and added-time goal proved enough to see the Germans advance at Toronto Stadium.\nGermany almost carved out the perfect start when Kai Havertz won a header from kick-off and fired the loose ball just over the crossbar.\nHe called upon Nadiem Amiri and Undav on the hour and just eight minutes later the former sent an inch-perfect cross for the latter to head in the leveller.\nKey stat: Deniz Undav now has nine goals from his last eight Germany caps.",
